<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
        Debug-only entitlements for TranscriptShadow.

        Production (Release) entitlements live in TranscriptShadow.entitlements
        and lock the app down with app-sandbox + the +5 EPIC-04b additions
        (cs.disable-library-validation, cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory,
        cs.allow-jit, files.user-selected.read-only, files.bookmarks.app-scope).

        Debug deliberately drops the sandbox so test code can exec the fake
        diarize shell scripts the integration suite generates. The Release
        codesign Run Script Build Phase (EPIC-04b CW3) signs the production
        bundle with TranscriptShadow.entitlements; this Debug file is only
        ever applied to Debug builds, and Debug is what xcodebuild test uses.

        Without this override, app-sandbox blocks `Process.run()` from
        launching scripts the test target writes to its temp dir, which
        prevents PyannoteSidecarDiarizationServiceTests from running.
    -->
</dict>
</plist>
